  "coach.routine.advancedTechnique.topSet": "Top set",
  "coach.routine.advancedTechnique.topSet.desc": "Your main heavy set for the day. After warm-up, perform one top set at the heaviest load you can handle for the target rep range with solid technique.\n\ne.g. On bench press, after build-up sets, your heaviest set of 5 reps at 100 kg.",
  "coach.routine.advancedTechnique.backOffSet": "Back-off set",
  "coach.routine.advancedTechnique.backOffSet.desc": "Sets performed after the top set. Reduce the load slightly (typically 10–20%) to accumulate more volume with controlled fatigue.\n\ne.g. If your top set was 100 kg, do the next 2 sets at 85 kg for 8–10 reps.",
  "coach.routine.advancedTechnique.clusterSets": "Cluster sets",
  "coach.routine.advancedTechnique.clusterSets.desc": "Split a normal set into small rep blocks with very short rests (10–30 s) between them. This lets you move a heavy load for more total reps than you could in one continuous set.\n\ne.g. Instead of 6 consecutive squat reps, do 2, rest 15 s, 2, rest 15 s, then the last 2.",
  "coach.routine.advancedTechnique.myoReps": "Myo-reps",
  "coach.routine.advancedTechnique.myoReps.desc": "Maximize fiber recruitment in little time. Perform an initial set near failure, rest 10–15 s, then do mini-sets of a few reps with the same load until you cannot hit the target number.\n\ne.g. 15 leg extension reps, rest 10 s, do 3, rest 10 s, do 3… until you can only do 2.",
  "coach.routine.advancedTechnique.dropSet": "Drop set",
  "coach.routine.advancedTechnique.dropSet.desc": "Push past initial failure. Work to failure, reduce the load (often 20–30%), and continue for as many reps as possible.\n\ne.g. Biceps curl with 20 kg to failure, grab 14 kg and keep repping.",

